1
00:00:00,757 --> 00:00:03,719
Oh, yeah, have you heard
about the campfire superstition?

2
00:00:03,802 --> 00:00:06,304
That if you confess to your crush,
you'll fall in love?

3
00:00:06,388 --> 00:00:08,181
I know it sounds kinda sketchy.

4
00:00:08,932 --> 00:00:10,434
Yeah, sketchy.

5
00:00:11,351 --> 00:00:13,687
But we're here anyway,
so why don't you try it?

6
00:00:14,354 --> 00:00:16,606
Maybe you'll finally
get an answer from him.

7
00:00:18,358 --> 00:00:19,443
[sighs softly]

8
00:00:19,526 --> 00:00:21,445
[mellow music playing]

9
00:00:21,528 --> 00:00:22,446
[inaudible]

10
00:00:29,828 --> 00:00:30,871
I won't.

11
00:00:38,545 --> 00:00:41,173
Until Taiki actually
falls in love with me,

12
00:00:41,798 --> 00:00:43,425
I don't need an answer.

13
00:00:45,010 --> 00:00:47,596
UEDA SHIKI HOTEL

14
00:00:49,222 --> 00:00:50,599
[girl] I've got it right here.

15
00:00:50,682 --> 00:00:51,725
[boy] Awesome, thanks.

16
00:00:54,394 --> 00:00:55,228
[gasps]

17
00:00:57,606 --> 00:00:59,149
[chuckling]

18
00:01:11,328 --> 00:01:13,914
[wind blowing]

19
00:01:14,873 --> 00:01:16,875
[opening theme song playing]

20
00:01:41,191 --> 00:01:44,611
BLUE BOX

21
00:02:44,629 --> 00:02:48,466
{\an8}EPISODE 24
A ROLLER COASTER

22
00:02:49,968 --> 00:02:51,011
[Hina] <i>Last night...</i>

23
00:02:52,053 --> 00:02:54,055
[serene music playing]

24
00:02:56,933 --> 00:02:59,227
[Taiki] I'm glad that woman was okay.

25
00:02:59,311 --> 00:03:00,770
[Chinatsu] Yeah, definitely.

26
00:03:01,313 --> 00:03:02,939
[Taiki] It got late, didn't it?

27
00:03:05,108 --> 00:03:07,402
[Hina] <i>I've known about it
from the beginning.</i>

28
00:03:11,406 --> 00:03:15,869
<i>I mean, I knew that Taiki liked Chinatsu
when I confessed to him.</i>

29
00:03:17,329 --> 00:03:18,455
[girl] Hina.

30
00:03:20,790 --> 00:03:22,542
[Hina] <i>This? This is no big deal.</i>

31
00:03:24,419 --> 00:03:25,795
I'll take this one.

32
00:03:26,338 --> 00:03:27,505
Yeah, thanks.

33
00:03:29,257 --> 00:03:32,344
[Hina] <i>It's not like
everything has been this painful.</i>

34
00:03:37,515 --> 00:03:39,226
<i>Like, when I confessed to him,</i>

35
00:03:39,309 --> 00:03:42,771
<i>that deer-in-headlights look he had,
it was priceless.</i>

36
00:03:43,730 --> 00:03:47,234
<i>When I get him to look at me,
as part of the great Hina's strategy,</i>

37
00:03:48,526 --> 00:03:50,362
{\an8}<i>and his face turns bright red...</i>

38
00:03:52,322 --> 00:03:54,032
{\an8}<i>some part of me explodes,</i>

39
00:03:54,908 --> 00:03:58,036
{\an8}<i>and all the little Hinas in my heart
have a dance party.</i>

40
00:04:02,207 --> 00:04:05,293
<i>When we put on</i> Snow White
<i>for the cultural festival...</i>

41
00:04:05,377 --> 00:04:07,045
SNOW WHITE SCRIPT

42
00:04:11,967 --> 00:04:13,051
THE PRINCE KISSES HER

43
00:04:13,134 --> 00:04:17,389
<i>...I fantasized about how it would be
if it were Taiki playing the prince.</i>

44
00:04:18,056 --> 00:04:18,890
[chuckles]

45
00:04:20,058 --> 00:04:21,893
<i>When that actually happened,</i>

46
00:04:21,977 --> 00:04:24,980
<i>I almost went crazy
because of how nervous I was.</i>

47
00:04:30,652 --> 00:04:34,322
<i>But in the end,
I'll never forget our scene together.</i>

48
00:04:37,993 --> 00:04:38,994
[music ends]

49
00:04:43,164 --> 00:04:44,916
<i>There's no way he understands...</i>

50
00:04:47,168 --> 00:04:48,420
<i>that that day...</i>

51
00:04:52,048 --> 00:04:54,384
I couldn't help
but imagine the real thing.

52
00:04:55,468 --> 00:04:57,429
Kissing you for real, Taiki.

53
00:04:58,054 --> 00:04:59,014
{\an8}What?

54
00:05:03,810 --> 00:05:05,812
[heart beating]

55
00:05:08,815 --> 00:05:10,191
Wanna do it for real?

56
00:05:16,698 --> 00:05:18,033
<i>I really thought</i>

57
00:05:18,700 --> 00:05:21,036
<i>I'd be okay with him kissing me.</i>

58
00:05:22,704 --> 00:05:26,958
<i>In the stillness of that classroom,
I felt hot all over.</i>

59
00:05:30,420 --> 00:05:33,631
<i>My heart was beating so fast, it hurt.</i>

60
00:05:35,550 --> 00:05:37,594
- [Taiki] Hina, watch out!
- Huh?

61
00:05:44,184 --> 00:05:45,477
[Hina] <i>During the play,</i>

62
00:05:46,644 --> 00:05:50,148
{\an8}<i>I was glad because I didn't want
my first kiss to be onstage.</i>

63
00:05:52,442 --> 00:05:55,361
<i>But after that,
so many people got involved.</i>

64
00:05:58,281 --> 00:06:02,285
<i>I think Taiki's reaction really meant
he was being considerate of me.</i>

65
00:06:03,620 --> 00:06:07,665
<i>But the truth is
I didn't completely hate the rumors.</i>

66
00:06:09,125 --> 00:06:10,293
<i>If anything...</i>

67
00:06:12,504 --> 00:06:16,257
<i>I was hoping they would lead
to the two of us dating.</i>

68
00:06:17,592 --> 00:06:21,429
<i>I wonder how it would feel
to actually date him.</i>

69
00:06:23,056 --> 00:06:26,267
<i>We'd walk home together, go to karaoke,</i>

70
00:06:26,893 --> 00:06:28,311
<i>take a ton of pictures...</i>

71
00:06:33,358 --> 00:06:34,943
<i>We'd even hold hands.</i>

72
00:06:37,362 --> 00:06:38,780
[gasps]

73
00:06:38,863 --> 00:06:40,448
[grunts]

74
00:06:44,369 --> 00:06:45,787
[sighs]

75
00:06:49,499 --> 00:06:50,792
[sighs]

76
00:06:50,875 --> 00:06:53,294
[all screaming]

77
00:06:55,505 --> 00:06:56,840
[Hina] <i>I guess I know now</i>

78
00:06:56,923 --> 00:06:59,801
<i>what it means
to be on an emotional roller coaster.</i>

79
00:07:06,349 --> 00:07:08,893
<i>Why doesn't he date me just to try it out?</i>

80
00:07:09,644 --> 00:07:12,188
<i>He could just use me and see how it goes.</i>

81
00:07:12,939 --> 00:07:14,816
<i>There are times I think like that.</i>

82
00:07:17,193 --> 00:07:19,821
<i>But he's sincere. I like that about him.</i>

83
00:07:20,572 --> 00:07:22,615
<i>He's not that kind of person.</i>

84
00:07:22,699 --> 00:07:24,284
<i>If I asked him those things,</i>

85
00:07:24,367 --> 00:07:27,704
<i>I don't think he could follow through
and hurt his friend so easily.</i>

86
00:07:30,832 --> 00:07:32,292
Meat's not ready yet.

87
00:07:32,375 --> 00:07:34,335
I'm not that big of an eater, come on.

88
00:07:35,420 --> 00:07:36,337
[gasps softly]

89
00:07:37,255 --> 00:07:38,840
{\an8}You have a leaf in your hair.

90
00:07:39,632 --> 00:07:41,342
{\an8}Oh? Where is it?

91
00:07:42,552 --> 00:07:44,387
- A bit higher.
- Mmm?

92
00:07:45,221 --> 00:07:46,347
No, it's further back.

93
00:07:47,015 --> 00:07:48,099
[Hina] Further?

94
00:07:50,310 --> 00:07:51,644
{\an8}Here. Let me help you.

95
00:07:56,441 --> 00:07:57,859
Dang, it's really in there.

96
00:07:59,861 --> 00:08:00,862
I like you.

97
00:08:02,405 --> 00:08:06,242
<i>But if I say that too much,
he'll probably get overwhelmed.</i>

98
00:08:07,368 --> 00:08:08,703
<i>Still...</i>

99
00:08:08,786 --> 00:08:10,205
[chuckles] I got it.

100
00:08:10,288 --> 00:08:12,749
[Hina] <i>You can't win a fight
if you don't throw a punch.</i>

101
00:08:12,832 --> 00:08:15,043
<i>I'll use the relationship we do have.</i>

102
00:08:16,085 --> 00:08:17,378
<i>Look at me.</i>

103
00:08:17,462 --> 00:08:18,546
[grunts softly]

104
00:08:19,464 --> 00:08:21,883
[Hina] <i>I don't wanna be
just his best friend anymore.</i>

105
00:08:23,134 --> 00:08:27,388
<i>It doesn't matter
if it's tomorrow, next week, next month.</i>

106
00:08:27,472 --> 00:08:29,432
<i>I'll wait as long as I have to.</i>

107
00:08:31,351 --> 00:08:32,519
<i>So, for now...</i>

108
00:08:33,269 --> 00:08:34,938
Look, there's one on you too!

109
00:08:35,021 --> 00:08:36,898
Only 'cause
you're trying to put it in my hair!

110
00:08:36,981 --> 00:08:39,567
[chuckles] No. Oh, what's that?

111
00:08:39,651 --> 00:08:41,778
- There's a big bug on you.
- Huh? Huh? Where?

112
00:08:41,861 --> 00:08:42,904
Just kidding.

113
00:08:42,987 --> 00:08:44,197
[Taiki] You get me every time.

114
00:08:44,280 --> 00:08:46,908
Well, would you look at that?
They get along so well.

115
00:08:48,159 --> 00:08:51,496
I've always admired couples
that act like friends with each other.

116
00:08:52,121 --> 00:08:55,416
Moriya, you like to play
with people's hearts, huh?

117
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,002
I wouldn't do something like that.

118
00:08:58,086 --> 00:09:01,422
And even if I did, the people I date
are usually okay with it.

119
00:09:01,506 --> 00:09:03,216
- [sighs]
- When it comes to love,

120
00:09:03,299 --> 00:09:06,302
the person being adored
is the one who's the happiest.

121
00:09:09,681 --> 00:09:12,725
So then, how does the other person
find happiness?

122
00:09:13,518 --> 00:09:14,435
What?

123
00:09:15,061 --> 00:09:17,438
In your love life, you get confessed to,

124
00:09:17,522 --> 00:09:19,524
but your relationships
never last, do they?

125
00:09:19,607 --> 00:09:20,441
I'm sorry, but...

126
00:09:22,068 --> 00:09:23,444
I'm not buying your method.

127
00:09:23,528 --> 00:09:24,988
{\an8}[Ayame] <i>What?!</i>

128
00:09:25,071 --> 00:09:26,447
{\an8}WHAT?!

129
00:09:26,531 --> 00:09:29,117
{\an8}<i>You think you can meddle
from the sideline, Four-eyes?</i>

130
00:09:29,200 --> 00:09:31,286
{\an8}<i>You don't even have a girlfriend, do you?</i>

131
00:09:35,540 --> 00:09:37,375
[grunts angrily]

132
00:09:39,377 --> 00:09:40,878
<i>I can't believe him!</i>

133
00:09:44,841 --> 00:09:46,301
[boy] This year's camp...

134
00:09:46,384 --> 00:09:48,011
is officially over!

135
00:09:49,053 --> 00:09:49,971
Let's light it!

136
00:09:51,055 --> 00:09:52,974
[all exclaiming]

137
00:09:53,057 --> 00:09:54,892
[girl] It's so pretty!

138
00:09:56,894 --> 00:09:58,896
[lighthearted music playing]

139
00:10:05,194 --> 00:10:06,029
BLEH

140
00:10:06,112 --> 00:10:06,946
Bleh!

141
00:10:07,655 --> 00:10:08,906
[Kyo grunts]

142
00:10:09,782 --> 00:10:10,825
[Ayame scoffs]

143
00:10:13,911 --> 00:10:15,079
[sighs]

144
00:10:16,539 --> 00:10:18,082
I'm not buying your method.

145
00:10:18,166 --> 00:10:19,751
[Ayame] <i>That's what he said.</i>

146
00:10:20,460 --> 00:10:23,588
<i>It is true that my relationships
have never lasted that long.</i>

147
00:10:24,339 --> 00:10:27,967
<i>Not to mention, I don't think
I've ever actually been in love.</i>

148
00:10:30,887 --> 00:10:32,597
<i>That is all the more reason...</i>

149
00:10:33,222 --> 00:10:36,351
{\an8}'Cause it's actually fun
having a crush on Taiki.

150
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:38,603
[Ayame] <i>...to help her!</i>

151
00:10:40,271 --> 00:10:42,106
[upbeat music playing]

152
00:10:43,441 --> 00:10:44,942
<i>Who on this planet</i>

153
00:10:45,735 --> 00:10:47,362
<i>wouldn't want to fight for...</i>

154
00:10:49,864 --> 00:10:52,241
<i>someone who loves with all their heart?</i>

155
00:10:54,118 --> 00:10:54,994
Oh?

156
00:10:55,912 --> 00:10:57,288
It's so cold.

157
00:10:57,372 --> 00:10:58,873
- No jacket?
- Nah.

158
00:10:59,415 --> 00:11:02,502
I left it in the gym earlier.
I'm gonna go grab it.

159
00:11:04,962 --> 00:11:06,005
[giggles]

160
00:11:07,882 --> 00:11:09,634
- Oh, Hina-bean!
- Huh?

161
00:11:10,343 --> 00:11:12,762
We're having a problem
with one of the cables,

162
00:11:13,596 --> 00:11:16,140
but, apparently,
they have some spares back in the gym.

163
00:11:16,224 --> 00:11:17,266
Could you get one for me?

164
00:11:17,850 --> 00:11:18,768
Sure thing.

165
00:11:18,851 --> 00:11:21,062
Oh, really? Thank you!

166
00:11:22,105 --> 00:11:23,147
{\an8}By the way,

167
00:11:23,898 --> 00:11:26,025
{\an8}you take as much time
as you need to, girl.

168
00:11:27,193 --> 00:11:28,194
[Hina] Hmm?

169
00:11:41,499 --> 00:11:42,542
Everything okay?

170
00:11:43,626 --> 00:11:44,919
Just getting equipment.

171
00:11:45,586 --> 00:11:47,797
'Cause Ayame asked for my help.

172
00:11:48,423 --> 00:11:50,675
Our manager is really demanding sometimes.

173
00:11:51,259 --> 00:11:52,093
{\an8}Huh?

174
00:11:52,176 --> 00:11:53,136
I'LL HELP YOU

175
00:11:53,219 --> 00:11:54,345
I wanna help you!

176
00:11:54,429 --> 00:11:55,513
TAKE ALL THE TIME YOU WANT!

177
00:11:55,596 --> 00:11:56,931
Take the time that you need.

178
00:11:58,266 --> 00:11:59,434
[Hina] She set this up.

179
00:12:00,226 --> 00:12:01,936
- [Taiki] What was it you needed?
- Uh...

180
00:12:03,354 --> 00:12:04,439
I can help.

181
00:12:05,273 --> 00:12:06,190
[gasps softly]

182
00:12:18,536 --> 00:12:19,454
It's not here.

183
00:12:20,163 --> 00:12:21,122
[Hina] Hmm.

184
00:12:22,957 --> 00:12:26,419
<i>It's possible Ayame was just
improvising the whole scenario.</i>

185
00:12:27,545 --> 00:12:28,463
[grunts]

186
00:12:31,549 --> 00:12:33,551
[lighthearted music playing distantly]

187
00:12:37,472 --> 00:12:38,556
Look at that.

188
00:12:39,390 --> 00:12:41,309
We have a good view of the campfire.

189
00:12:42,059 --> 00:12:43,561
- Oh, yeah.
- [gasps]

190
00:12:43,644 --> 00:12:45,521
It's even more magical up here.

191
00:12:52,987 --> 00:12:55,323
Oh, of course Nishida's dancing.

192
00:12:58,618 --> 00:13:00,495
Let's watch from here for a while.

193
00:13:00,578 --> 00:13:01,412
[gasps]

194
00:13:09,587 --> 00:13:11,255
Now that you mention it, I am tired.

195
00:13:12,173 --> 00:13:13,508
Why don't we take a break?

196
00:13:15,843 --> 00:13:16,802
[sighs]

197
00:13:23,309 --> 00:13:24,602
[Hina chuckles]

198
00:13:24,685 --> 00:13:27,939
So even the amazing Taiki
who runs nonstop all year round

199
00:13:28,022 --> 00:13:29,065
gets tired too.

200
00:13:29,774 --> 00:13:30,775
You're making fun of me.

201
00:13:31,734 --> 00:13:32,902
The energy I expend

202
00:13:32,985 --> 00:13:35,821
differs from a certain someone
who travels by bus.

203
00:13:35,905 --> 00:13:38,032
I will have you know we ran every morning.

204
00:13:39,033 --> 00:13:40,034
That reminds me.

205
00:13:40,117 --> 00:13:40,952
YAMANONAKA HOTEL

206
00:13:41,035 --> 00:13:42,620
Third year of junior high school,

207
00:13:42,703 --> 00:13:45,540
you snuck out of the hotel
where we were staying on our school trip

208
00:13:45,623 --> 00:13:46,791
for a morning run.

209
00:13:47,583 --> 00:13:49,085
It's part of my routine.

210
00:13:49,669 --> 00:13:51,796
{\an8}Yeah, but you got in trouble, right?

211
00:13:51,879 --> 00:13:54,799
The teacher only found out
'cause everyone teased me about it.

212
00:13:55,466 --> 00:13:57,927
And remember that time
during the second-year camping trip

213
00:13:58,010 --> 00:13:59,804
where we all played Cops and Robbers?

214
00:13:59,887 --> 00:14:00,721
SMUG

215
00:14:00,805 --> 00:14:03,558
Oh, when I avoided everybody till the end?

216
00:14:03,641 --> 00:14:04,475
SHADOW CLONES

217
00:14:04,559 --> 00:14:05,434
Uh-huh.

218
00:14:05,518 --> 00:14:08,312
All your fancy footwork cracked me up.

219
00:14:08,813 --> 00:14:09,814
Is that a compliment?

220
00:14:10,690 --> 00:14:12,233
Don't think I didn't see you.

221
00:14:12,859 --> 00:14:14,819
How you were the very first one
to get captured

222
00:14:14,902 --> 00:14:16,320
and then had nothing to do.

223
00:14:16,404 --> 00:14:18,406
{\an8}I got caught 'cause of my shoelaces.

224
00:14:18,489 --> 00:14:20,241
{\an8}Yeah, okay.

225
00:14:21,033 --> 00:14:23,828
Even a cat knows
it must hide its claws sometimes.

226
00:14:23,911 --> 00:14:25,997
[Taiki laughs]

227
00:14:26,664 --> 00:14:29,834
But you got captured right away
during the second round too.

228
00:14:32,962 --> 00:14:36,299
And you couldn't even tell
that they were trying to let you escape.

229
00:14:37,842 --> 00:14:38,676
[gasps]

230
00:14:43,848 --> 00:14:45,266
[Hina] Hey, Taiki.

231
00:14:45,808 --> 00:14:46,809
[Taiki grunts]

232
00:14:49,103 --> 00:14:51,188
[Hina] There's something I wanna ask you.

233
00:14:51,731 --> 00:14:52,773
[Taiki] What is it?

234
00:14:54,483 --> 00:14:56,444
{\an8}[Hina] During the King's Card Game...

235
00:14:57,528 --> 00:14:58,446
{\an8}[Taiki] Uh-huh.

236
00:15:00,990 --> 00:15:03,618
[Hina] What was your actual answer
going to be?

237
00:15:07,496 --> 00:15:08,915
For a minute there, it seemed

238
00:15:08,998 --> 00:15:11,626
you were going to spill the beans
about liking Chinatsu!

239
00:15:13,377 --> 00:15:16,297
But surprisingly,
you're more of a chicken than I thought.

240
00:15:17,256 --> 00:15:18,257
[chuckles softly]

241
00:15:18,341 --> 00:15:22,261
But I guess you're not the kind of guy
who blurts out his feelings like that.

242
00:15:25,348 --> 00:15:28,392
Oh! But of course
you can confess if you want.

243
00:15:28,476 --> 00:15:30,603
That's been our deal from the beginning.

244
00:15:32,730 --> 00:15:35,107
I'm totally fine with that.

245
00:15:35,942 --> 00:15:38,235
I just need to try harder than you.

246
00:15:39,320 --> 00:15:40,529
To be honest,

247
00:15:41,155 --> 00:15:43,157
sometimes all of this stings a bit,

248
00:15:44,450 --> 00:15:46,911
but it's nothing to worry yourself over.

249
00:15:48,204 --> 00:15:51,290
{\an8}It's all fine because I love you.

250
00:15:52,500 --> 00:15:53,501
[gasps]

251
00:16:02,510 --> 00:16:04,512
[wind blowing]

252
00:16:15,147 --> 00:16:17,149
Welp. Should we head back?

253
00:16:17,233 --> 00:16:19,777
I should tell Ayame
we couldn't find the equipment.

254
00:16:21,237 --> 00:16:23,280
[sighs] <i>Why did I just say that?</i>

255
00:16:23,364 --> 00:16:25,700
<i>I wasn't planning
on telling him I love him.</i>

256
00:16:29,662 --> 00:16:30,496
Hina.

257
00:16:43,175 --> 00:16:44,010
[Hina] Hmm?

258
00:16:46,804 --> 00:16:47,722
Sorry.

259
00:16:47,805 --> 00:16:49,724
[heart beating]

260
00:16:56,522 --> 00:16:57,648
[Hina] You're sorry?

261
00:16:58,733 --> 00:16:59,734
About what?

262
00:16:59,817 --> 00:17:01,819
[wind blowing]

263
00:17:04,822 --> 00:17:07,742
[Taiki] I can't... go out with you.

264
00:17:14,081 --> 00:17:16,083
["Shade of Love"
by Takashi Ohmama playing]

265
00:17:21,881 --> 00:17:22,798
{\an8}Nuh-uh.

266
00:17:24,675 --> 00:17:26,635
I told you that I don't need an answer.

267
00:17:27,136 --> 00:17:28,804
There's no need to rush it.

268
00:17:30,848 --> 00:17:33,768
It's not as if you and Chinatsu
have started dating, right?

269
00:17:34,727 --> 00:17:36,937
[Taiki] We haven't. But...

270
00:17:38,773 --> 00:17:41,275
[Hina] Exactly. So you don't need
to give me an answer yet.

271
00:17:42,193 --> 00:17:45,488
{\an8}I'm not going to complain,
no matter how long it takes.

272
00:17:46,030 --> 00:17:47,364
{\an8}Reject me now,

273
00:17:47,448 --> 00:17:50,701
{\an8}and then when you come to like me later,
you'll regret it.

274
00:17:52,870 --> 00:17:54,038
Even so,

275
00:17:54,997 --> 00:17:57,583
I don't think
our relationship's working right now.

276
00:17:59,293 --> 00:18:03,506
I know you've said that it's okay
if I go after Chinatsu instead.

277
00:18:04,298 --> 00:18:07,301
But I haven't been able to face her
with honesty

278
00:18:07,384 --> 00:18:10,304
because of this situation.

279
00:18:11,430 --> 00:18:17,103
And even though I like Chinatsu,
I've been swayed by you, and I feel awful.

280
00:18:17,895 --> 00:18:22,233
I think my indecisiveness
is ultimately hurting you, Hina.

281
00:18:23,984 --> 00:18:26,821
That's why
I want to make things clear now.

282
00:18:26,904 --> 00:18:28,072
The two of us should...

283
00:18:33,702 --> 00:18:35,579
{\an8}I told you that I'm fine with it!

284
00:18:36,247 --> 00:18:39,291
I confessed to you
even though you like someone else.

285
00:18:40,167 --> 00:18:42,211
It may be that you like Chinatsu,

286
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:45,589
but it doesn't change
the fact that I like you.

287
00:18:47,174 --> 00:18:49,093
{\an8}That's not how this is supposed to work.

288
00:18:50,010 --> 00:18:51,428
{\an8}I don't care!

289
00:18:51,512 --> 00:18:54,598
{\an8}Everything is gonna be worth it
when I get you to like me!

290
00:18:55,724 --> 00:18:58,602
{\an8}Hina, I don't feel the same way about you.

291
00:18:58,686 --> 00:18:59,728
{\an8}Why not?

292
00:19:01,313 --> 00:19:05,067
{\an8}Chinatsu doesn't have
as many memories with you as I do.

293
00:19:06,735 --> 00:19:10,072
Is it 'cause we don't live together?
We can start doing that.

294
00:19:12,658 --> 00:19:15,995
It's not for me to know
how Chinatsu really feels about you.

295
00:19:17,204 --> 00:19:18,706
- But I feel--
- Hina...

296
00:19:21,250 --> 00:19:23,252
The person I like isn't going to change.

297
00:19:23,836 --> 00:19:24,837
[gasps]

298
00:19:29,717 --> 00:19:30,759
[sniffles]

299
00:19:32,636 --> 00:19:34,388
- [sobs]
- Hina...

300
00:19:42,771 --> 00:19:43,772
[song ends]

301
00:19:45,399 --> 00:19:47,902
[humming]

302
00:19:48,694 --> 00:19:51,155
[chuckles] I wonder if things went well.

303
00:19:51,780 --> 00:19:55,784
Just the two of them alone in a gym,
dimly lit by the campfire.

304
00:19:56,785 --> 00:19:59,121
And there was
a superstition or something too.

305
00:19:59,747 --> 00:20:02,291
I bet it set a really romantic mood.

306
00:20:04,418 --> 00:20:05,836
[grunts] Uh?

307
00:20:07,379 --> 00:20:08,422
Hina-bean?

308
00:20:12,885 --> 00:20:14,720
[sobs quietly]

309
00:20:20,726 --> 00:20:21,810
[Ayame] Are you okay?

310
00:20:23,437 --> 00:20:25,814
- Wait, did something--
- [Hina continues sobbing]

311
00:20:27,650 --> 00:20:28,859
[Ayame] <i>She's crying.</i>

312
00:20:30,903 --> 00:20:33,322
He said he can't go out with me.

313
00:20:33,405 --> 00:20:34,323
[gasps]

314
00:20:37,868 --> 00:20:39,870
That he has feelings for someone else.

315
00:20:41,413 --> 00:20:43,499
[mellow music playing]

316
00:20:43,582 --> 00:20:45,834
And even if she doesn't like him back,

317
00:20:47,419 --> 00:20:50,089
that the person he likes
isn't going to change!

318
00:20:51,423 --> 00:20:53,842
[crying]

319
00:21:01,850 --> 00:21:03,435
[Hina] <i>In rhythmic gymnastics,</i>

320
00:21:03,936 --> 00:21:07,189
<i>there are some people
who believe that hard work pays off,</i>

321
00:21:07,815 --> 00:21:11,443
<i>and there are other people
who say that isn't always true.</i>

322
00:21:15,990 --> 00:21:18,325
<i>My hard work has always paid off.</i>

323
00:21:20,369 --> 00:21:23,872
<i>And I've come to like myself
because I've never stopped trying.</i>

324
00:21:23,956 --> 00:21:24,873
[all exclaiming]

325
00:21:25,916 --> 00:21:26,834
[Hina] <i>But...</i>

326
00:21:28,627 --> 00:21:30,379
<i>when it comes to love...</i>

327
00:21:30,462 --> 00:21:33,299
[indistinct chatter, laughter]

328
00:21:37,928 --> 00:21:39,138
[Chinatsu sighs]

329
00:21:42,141 --> 00:21:43,892
[wind blowing]

330
00:21:51,984 --> 00:21:53,402
[Hina sobs]

331
00:21:54,153 --> 00:21:56,155
[bawling]

332
00:22:01,577 --> 00:22:03,203
[Hina] <i>...why am I so pathetic?</i>

333
00:22:05,497 --> 00:22:07,499
[closing theme song playing]
